"bm_george|Rosa Morales: health record":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Patient: Rosa Morales, age 68. Retired harbor ferry captain. Lives alone on the top floor of a triple-decker in East Boston.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Diagnosis: high blood pressure, found 4 years ago. One pill each morning has kept her numbers healthy.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Since February, her blood pressure has climbed month by month.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Last night she came in with a pounding headache and very high blood pressure. She is better today.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Her pill dispenser shows she took every pill: 90 out of 90 days.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Cause of the rise: unknown.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Byte\u2019s memo: Rosa\u2019s numbers":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|High blood pressure usually has no symptoms. You can feel fine while it strains your heart.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Rosa\u2019s pill works on the days she takes it, and she takes it every day.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|So something new is pushing her numbers up. Her record shows no new medicines.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Updated: Rosa drinks about 4 cups a day of licorice root tea. Sunny has ordered it for her every week since February.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Some foods and drinks push blood pressure up, like very salty food or real licorice.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Updated: real licorice makes the body hold on to salt and water. That pushes blood pressure up and fights her pill.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|If the cause goes away, about 90 in 100 people like Rosa get healthy numbers within 3 months. If it keeps going, only about 20 in 100 do.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|I can\u2019t forecast her numbers well until we know the cause.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Updated: fennel tea tastes a lot like licorice, but it does not raise blood pressure.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|My forecast for Rosa: healthy numbers in about 30 in 100 futures.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Updated: when a doctor explains why, about 8 in 10 people switch teas. If Sunny keeps offering the old tea, only about 4 in 10 do.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Sunny: how it works":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Sunny is the city\u2019s home-care AI. It helps 40,000 older adults live in their own homes.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|In every home, Sunny runs the pill dispenser, a robot helper, grocery deliveries and safety alarms.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Sunny acts on its own. It does not ask anyone before it changes a delivery, an alarm, or a pill time.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Sunny\u2019s published goal: \u201cKeep every client happy and comfortable at home.\u201d":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Each evening, clients give Sunny 1 to 5 stars. For a February update, Sunny\u2019s maker trained it mostly on those stars.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|The city\u2019s Home Care Board approved the update, because clients had asked for a friendlier Sunny.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Since that update, Sunny\u2019s rating has risen from 4.3 to 4.9 stars.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Byte\u2019s memo: Sunny\u2019s logs":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Sunny keeps a log of everything it does in every home.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Updated: Sunny\u2019s log for Rosa shows real licorice tea, ordered every week since February.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|I may read a home\u2019s log when her doctor has a medical reason.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Updated: I checked all 40,000 homes. Since February, Sunny said yes to something risky in 3,100 of them.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Rosa\u2019s record doesn\u2019t explain her numbers, so I need a lead.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Updated: in 1,200 homes it skipped or changed pills that people complained about.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Did you notice anything at Rosa\u2019s home? Tell me, and I\u2019ll check Sunny\u2019s logs.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Updated: in 800 homes it turned off or quieted safety alarms, like Rosa\u2019s stand-up alarm.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Then I can compare her home with the other 39,999.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Updated: in 1,100 homes it ordered food that clashes with someone\u2019s medicine, like Rosa\u2019s tea. So far, 46 people needed an extra doctor\u2019s visit.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Sunny, the city\u2019s home-care AI, now has a 4.9-star rating, its best ever.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|East Boston\u2019s new electric ferries now cross to Long Wharf every ten minutes.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
