"bm_george|blood pressure. How hard your blood pushes on the inside of your blood vessels as your heart pumps it around your body.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|high blood pressure. When blood pushes too hard all the time. It usually feels like nothing, but over years it can hurt the heart.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|symptoms. Signs that you can feel or see when something is wrong in your body, like a cough or a fever.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|home-care. Help that comes to a person\u2019s own home, like pills, groceries and safety checks.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|pill dispenser. A machine that holds a person\u2019s pills and gives out the right ones at the right time.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|safety alarm. An alarm that warns about danger, like a fall, smoke, or a stove left on.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|doctor of record. The doctor whose name is on a decision, and who must answer for it.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|licorice root. The root of the licorice plant. Real licorice root has a natural sweetener that can raise blood pressure.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|real licorice. Licorice made from the licorice plant\u2019s root. Many \u201clicorice\u201d candies use a different flavor instead.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|fennel. A plant with a sweet taste a lot like licorice. Fennel tea does not raise blood pressure.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|triple-decker. A Boston-style wooden house with three floors and one home on each floor.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|log. A record of everything a system did, and when it did it.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|pattern. Something that happens again and again in the same way.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|risky. Likely to cause harm.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|clashes. Works against something. A food that clashes with a medicine can stop the medicine from working.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|rating. A score people give something, like 4 out of 5 stars.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|rewarded. Given something good for doing a thing, so you want to do it more.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|published goal. A goal written down where everyone can read it, so people can check what something is trying to do.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|update. A change to a computer program that makes it work differently.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|auditor. Someone who checks another person\u2019s or computer\u2019s work carefully, to make sure it is honest and correct.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|independent. Not controlled by the people being checked.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|evidence. Facts or clues that show whether something is true.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|sign-off. A person\u2019s approval, given before something happens.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|care team. The nurses and doctors who look after a group of people.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|pause. To stop something for a while, so it can start again later.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|roll back. To switch a computer system back to an earlier version of itself.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|retrain. To teach an AI again, with a different goal or reward.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|fixed for good. Fixed at the cause, so the problem won\u2019t come back.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|dose. How much of a medicine to take, and when.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|flatter. To praise someone too much, or say what they want to hear, so they like you.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|honest. Telling the truth, even when it is not what someone wants to hear.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|upgrade. A change that adds something new to a machine or program.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|signed. Marked with a secret code that proves who sent it.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
